# The committed bytes ARE the evidence here, so nothing in this directory may
# be normalized on the way into or out of the object store.
#
# The repository root sets `* text=auto eol=lf`, which exists for a good reason
# (DB6-S27: CRLF leaking into dollar-quoted PL/pgSQL bodies broke the schema
# fingerprint). But upstream Inter's `LICENSE.txt` ships with CRLF, so that rule
# would rewrite it — and `FONT-PROVENANCE.json` records the SHA-256 of the
# *upstream* bytes. A normalized checkout would hash differently, failing
# `node tools/check-app3-f01-font-assets.mjs` on any clean clone while the file
# looked untouched in a diff.
#
# `-text` disables all conversion. The WOFF2 binaries are already safe by
# content detection; this makes that guarantee explicit rather than incidental.
* -text
